# ENG-019. `union` keeps the lines from both sides of a conflicting hunk instead
# of raising a conflict. That is the wrong behaviour for almost every file and
# the right one for exactly these: they are append-only lists of independent
# rows, generated from one-file-per-task sources, where the correct resolution
# is always "keep both". A union merge can still leave rows out of order or
# duplicated, which `npm run tasks:check` catches and `npm run tasks:build`
# fixes — a command instead of a hand-resolved conflict.
#
# Do NOT extend this to prose. Union-merging a paragraph produces text that
# reads as though someone wrote it, and nobody did.
tasks/INDEX.md merge=union
